# C040 — closing the tester->backend loop on the journeys arc (C038 vocabulary/gaps + C039 hatches). FOUR pieces:
# P1 Scenario-Outline generator + outline-aware parse/emit; P2 example precedence resolver; P3 generic @suluk/stubgen
# (contract stub + handler via an adapter seam); P4 promote-into-Zod (the tester-curated public example lands in the Zod
# source as .meta({examples}), so Zod stays the single traceable home for every example). Operator decided the three
# forks: (1) promote into Zod, (2) all inside @suluk/journeys, (3) a generic @suluk/stubgen now. ORIGINATED + the
# tester-UX and the source-writing promote step UNWITNESSED => honestly LOW ceilings (aggregate ~0.45). v1 witnesses ONLY
# the P2 resolver + the wall; P1/P3/P4 are designed, not yet built.

# EXAMPLE PRECEDENCE (P2, the witnessed slice). resolveExample(schema, {public?, maintainer?}, hint) resolves a field/
# body example by precedence public > maintainer (explicit, or the schema's own examples/example/const) > synthetic, and
# stamps {tier, synthetic, provenance}. Tier 1 is a DETERMINISTIC schema synthesizer honoring const/enum/default/format/
# length/numeric-bounds — NO external faker dep in v1 (a recorded deviation from the operator's "take the faker dep"
# framing): deterministic => BDD tests don't flap, and a synthetic value is ALWAYS lowest-precedence + always overridable
# + carries synthetic:true, which IS the reconciliation with the arc's never-launder discipline. WITNESSED by
# tooling/ts/packages/journeys/test/examples.test.ts (precedence order, determinism, type/format/bounds honoring).
claim examples_precedence_public_over_maintainer_over_synthetic: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when examples_precedence_public_over_maintainer_over_synthetic == False

# NEVER-LAUNDER VIA PRECEDENCE. The synthesizer never presents a value as authoritative: tier "synthetic" is only ever
# reached when NO public and NO maintainer/schema example exists, and the result carries synthetic:true so every
# downstream (outline seed rows, docs, the runnable suite) can label it honestly. This keeps faker-style synthesis on the
# right side of the discipline the SDK/journeys emitters already hold ("provide input" placeholders, never invented
# values presented as real). WITNESSED by test/examples.test.ts (synthetic flag true ONLY when synthesized).
claim examples_synthetic_is_lowest_and_marked: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when examples_synthetic_is_lowest_and_marked == False

# THE VALUE WALL (rides C038/C039). Examples are VALUES, so (a) they stay as .example/examples annotations and NEVER
# enter the static matcher — buildAda/matchRequest are invariant to any example; NO x-suluk-* facet is minted; and (b)
# the value-synthesis layer (examples.ts + the future outline emitter) is walled off from the PURE PROJECTOR CORE
# (vocabulary.ts/bind.ts/gherkin.ts/normalize.ts), which must not import it. examples.ts is self-contained (no
# journeys-internal, no external import) so it stays a one-file extraction if @suluk/reference / @suluk/sdk later want
# the resolver. WITNESSED by test/examples-wall.test.ts (a source-level forbidden-import gate cloning hatch-wall.test.ts).
claim examples_value_wall_core_never_imports: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when examples_value_wall_core_never_imports == False

# SCENARIO OUTLINES (P1, GENERATOR + PARSER-CAPTURE BUILT 2026-06-30). buildScenarioOutlines/renderScenarioOutlines
# (journeys/src/outline.ts) emit, per operation, a Scenario Outline whose Examples columns are the CLIENT-FACING input
# fields (computed dropped via C041 origin) and whose seed row comes from the resolver: an `input` cell = a synthesized
# value; a `sourced` cell = the WIRING TOKEN <op.select> (not a value). gherkin.ts (which tokenized Scenario Outline /
# Examples but DROPPED the table) now CAPTURES the table into Scenario.examples {headers, rows} — and a LATENT parser bug
# was fixed (the KW alternation listed Scenario before Scenario Outline, so "Scenario Outline: x" mis-parsed as name
# "Outline: x"; reordered longest-first). WITNESSED by journeys/test/outline.test.ts (generation + computed-dropped +
# sourced-token + render->parse round-trip). RUNNABLE HALF BUILT 2026-06-30: emit.ts unrolls ONE bun:test per Examples
# row; the outline's When is the contract's bindable vocabulary phrase (so it binds) and the Examples columns carry the
# bound When op's request body by NAME; an `input` cell -> a coerced literal, a `sourced` cell <op.select> -> pick(
# captured, op, select) (resolveSourced's shape, inlined) resolving from a prior step's CAPTURED result -> end-to-end
# chaining across a multi-step journey (each bound When captured under its op.name). Ops with path/query args fall back to
# the provide-input placeholder (not yet outline-wired). WITNESSED by journeys/test/emit-outline.test.ts (rows unrolled,
# body-from-row, sourced chaining, capture) + the visual suite (client.subscription.create({plan:"pro"}) ->
# captured["createSubscription"] -> client.charge({amountCents:100, subscriptionId: pick(...)})). Ceiling stays modest:
# the "is an Examples table intuitive to a real QA" question is the C038 residual-open, still unwitnessed.
claim outlines_runnable_with_sourced_chaining: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when outlines_runnable_with_sourced_chaining == False

# STUBGEN (P3, BUILT 2026-06-30). NEW zero-dep package @suluk/stubgen emits the CONTRACT half generically (a RouteContract
# literal — the @suluk/hono shape — name/method/path inferred from the intent, request Zod inferred from the Examples
# columns' sample cells, every inference // TODO: tighten) and the HANDLER half through a HandlerTarget ADAPTER SEAM
# (mirroring @suluk/deploy DeployProvider / C034 AgentRuntimeProvider): honoEffectTarget = toolfactory's Effect + run() +
# RouteError<name> idiom (the first adapter), honoTarget = a framework-generic fallback. stubSpec/renderContract/
# generateStub(s). The inferred Zod is LOSSY by construction; the maintainer owns the final schema (never laundered —
# emitted with TODO markers). @suluk/core never imports @suluk/stubgen — TEST-ENFORCED by stubgen/test/wall.test.ts
# (also pins the zero-dep leaf). WITNESSED by stubgen/test/stubgen.test.ts (inference, render, both targets) + the visual
# stub. FOLLOW-ON: a journeys helper to derive StubGaps from a GapReport's NEEDS-CONTRACT + the outline columns; toolfactory wiring.
claim stubgen_generic_contract_plus_handler_seam_built: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when stubgen_generic_contract_plus_handler_seam_built == False

# PROMOTE-INTO-ZOD (P4, PURE CORE BUILT 2026-06-30; operator fork #1). A tester marks an Examples block @public (the
# parser now captures @-tags); promote.ts lifts the block's first row into the matching Zod schema's SOURCE as
# .meta({examples:[...]}), provenance-stamped, so ZOD IS THE LITERAL HOME for every example (and the value flows into the
# rendered docs as the request .example). The source-write is SAFE: MARKED (@suluk-public), IDEMPOTENT (re-promote
# REPLACES the marked block via a string-aware paren scan, never double-appends), and NEVER CLOBBERS a hand-authored
# top-level .meta({examples}) (it REFUSES) — and a PROPERTY-level .meta is not mistaken for the top-level example meta.
# Pieces: extractPublicRows + buildExampleObject (typed coercion, wiring-token skipped) + promoteExampleIntoZod (the
# surgery) + promoteFeatureExamples (orchestrator, target injected per the app's scenario->schemaVar map). WITNESSED by
# journeys/test/promote.test.ts (append/idempotent/refuse-clobber/property-meta-safe/orchestrate). FOLLOW-ON: the live bin
# (read feature+source, resolve target from the contract, run mizan_check_action_safety BEFORE writing, write + git-diff
# review) + toolfactory wiring. The pure source-write is built + tested; the live file-IO + mizan gate are the consumer's.
claim promote_public_example_into_zod_source_core_built: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when promote_public_example_into_zod_source_core_built == False
